{"name":"Fragile Blue","hex":"#cfd1d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fragile","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily broken, not sturdy; of delicate material.","Readily disrupted or destroyed."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something that is fragile."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragile"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fragile (Yes album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fragile is the fourth studio album by the English progressive rock band Yes, released in the United Kingdom on 12 November 1971 and in the United States on 4 January 1972 by Atlantic Records. The record marked the studio debut of keyboardist Rick Wakeman, who replaced founding member Tony Kaye following the promotional tour for the band's breakthrough release, The Yes Album (1971)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Fragile_%28Yes_album%29_cover_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fragile_(Yes_album)"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Yes_1973_press_photo_%28cropped%29_-_Rick_Wakeman.jpg/330px-Yes_1973_press_photo_%28cropped%29_-_Rick_Wakeman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Yes_1973_press_photo_%28cropped%29_-_Rick_Wakeman.jpg/330px-Yes_1973_press_photo_%28cropped%29_-_Rick_Wakeman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fragile was the band's first album to feature keyboardist Rick Wakeman (pictured in 1973)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYes_1973_press_photo_(cropped)_-_Rick_Wakeman.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/1956_Gibson_ES-5_Switchmaster_-_Carl_Perkins%27_-_Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame%2C_Cleveland%2C_OH_%282018-08-31_by_Claude_Humbert%29.jpg/500px-1956_Gibson_ES-5_Switchmaster_-_Carl_Perkins%27_-_Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame%2C_Cleveland%2C_OH_%282018-08-31_by_Claude_Humbert%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/1956_Gibson_ES-5_Switchmaster_-_Carl_Perkins%27_-_Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame%2C_Cleveland%2C_OH_%282018-08-31_by_Claude_Humbert%29.jpg/1280px-1956_Gibson_ES-5_Switchmaster_-_Carl_Perkins%27_-_Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame%2C_Cleveland%2C_OH_%282018-08-31_by_Claude_Humbert%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/1956_